add('Matching bands and versioned ultimate shanks','CSMatchingShank independently normalizes profiles and applies start/middle/end wall-drop overrides before generating matching-band geometry. Old CSUltimateShank1 reads positional nested arrays for gem size, parameters, transform and profile, then feeds BuildChannel. Their data contracts differ from simple finished mesh placement.',[E('CSBlocks.Shank.Matching/CSMatchingShank.cs','InOverrideChannelWallDropStart.GetValue','CSMatchingShank.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Shank.Obsolete/CSUltimateShank1.cs','GemInfoUltimateShank gemInfoUltimateShank','CSUltimateShank1.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Shank.Obsolete/CSUltimateShank1.cs','OutSurfaceOutput.SetData(BuildChannel','CSUltimateShank1.Update')],K.concat(['matching gem/shank channel layouts','legacy nested array contracts']),'retain-versioned-local-algorithms',['Open matching-band fixtures with independent start/mid/end drop; compare distance to center ring and profile outputs.','Load each UltimateShank and UltimateMatchingShank GUID fixture, edit gem row and compare old generated surfaces and nested data shape.'],['Body audit covers representative old/current implementations; exact old channel layouts must remain stable.']);
add('French shank mesh/BRep part deformation','CSFrenchShank exits early for production display, otherwise separates BRep, mesh and curve parts, constructs tagged start/center/end CSFrenchGeometry pieces according to open/closed gem loop, validates top/base/side parts and consumes UltimateGemData. Later it forms edge/Z/gem curves and emits channel parts and edge curves.',[E('CSBlocks.Shank.French/CSFrenchShank.cs','public override bool Update()','CSFrenchShank.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Shank.French/CSFrenchShank.cs','CSFourRailSweep.FindMinMax','CSFrenchShank.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Shank.French/CSFrenchShank.cs','OutChannel.SetData','CSFrenchShank.Update')],K.concat(['named/tagged French geometry assets','CSFourRailSweep','CAM mode']),'local-kernel-and-part-assets-required',['Load BRep and mesh French-part fixtures with start/center/end tags; vary edge thickness at all positions and compare transitions.','Test closed gem loop, missing top/base/side assets and production-show toggle; compare outputs and errors.']);
add('French halo display and production tooling','CSFrenchHaloSet skips when production is shown, builds gem rails from sorted gems, accepts mesh/BRep French parts and computes upper/lower rails with independent corner blends/scales. CSFrenchHaloProduction has its own production/underlying-surface gate and emits channel/shank profiles, base/loft, scallop, graver, gem and pilot-hole cutters.',[E('CSBlocks.Settings.FrenchHalo/CSFrenchHaloSet.cs','public override bool Update()','CSFrenchHaloSet.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Settings.FrenchHalo/CSFrenchHaloSet.cs','CSFrenchHaloHelper.CalculateRail','CSFrenchHaloSet.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Settings.FrenchHalo/CSFrenchHaloProduction.cs','public override bool Update()','CSFrenchHaloProduction.Update')],K.concat(['French named part assets','CSFrenchHaloHelper/morphs','production cutter templates','CAM mode']),'local-kernel-and-part-assets-required',['Produce round and pointed French halos in display and production modes; compare rail corner continuity, scallops, pilot holes and cutter positions.','Toggle boolean/divot/underlying surfaces and vary wall thickness, profile size and cluster angle; compare each named output family.'],['Full production boolean loops and obsolete French variants remain fixture-validation gaps.']);
add('Linked gem/profile/collar sequences','CSLinkedGemRowOnRingRail orients at normalized rail start, uses prior right point/vector when present to derive continuity transform, computes spacing from rotated gem bounds, duplicates a requested count and emits right-point/right-vector for the next linked section.',[E('CSBlocks.Linked/CSLinkedGemRowOnRingRail.cs','public override bool Update()','CSLinkedGemRowOnRingRail.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Linked/CSLinkedGemRowOnRingRail.cs','OutRightRailPoint.SetData','CSLinkedGemRowOnRingRail.Update')],K.concat(['linked predecessor outputs','normalized arc-length framing']),'local-kernel-required',['Chain two linked gem rows of unequal sizes/rotation/spacing; verify endpoint/vector handoff and no discontinuity after changing first row.','Remove predecessor point/vector and verify identity fallback; include old linked GUID fixture corpus.'],['Other linked collar/profile/space/start nodes are indexed, not separately body-validated.']);
add('Gem/prong channel builder mode and width loopback','CSGemInChannelSetUp switches prong versus channel spacing/wall-drop inputs, requires profile and gem definition, rotates the gem and determines whether profile width/wall spacing changes require gem size recalculation. It emits profile/gem sizes and loopback values used by downstream builders.',[E('CSBlocks.Builders/CSGemInChannelSetUp.cs','public override bool Update()','CSGemInChannelSetUp.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Builders/CSGemInChannelSetUp.cs','if (num || flag || flag2)','CSGemInChannelSetUp.Update')],K.concat(['gem table scaling','graph update markers/loopback']),'local-kernel-and-graph-semantics-required',['Toggle channel/prong mode while holding geometry fixed; compare effective gem spacing, wall drop and loopback profile width/gem size.','Change profile width then gem size separately and compare dependency-update order with PC.']);
add('Gem seat/cutter solids','CSGemCutter converts each gem to local unscaled coordinates, produces girdle/top/seat/bottom outlines with Z offsets, clamps scale to .01 and lofts four sections straight with caps, then transforms cutter back to world.',[E('CSBlocks.Cutters/CSGemCutter.cs','public override bool Update()','CSGemCutter.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Cutters/CSGemCutter.cs','CSUtilSweepRC.Loft(new Curve[4]','CSGemCutter.Update')],K.concat(['gem outline and unscaled transforms']),'local-kernel-required',['Generate seat cutters for round and elongated gems with positive/negative spacing and distinct top/seat/bottom offsets; compare capped solid volume and placement.','Use offsets that would collapse the cutter; confirm .01 clamp and behavior of invalid gems.'],['Azure/box/bezel/channel/halo/micropave/pattern/scallop/shank cutters have separate indexed identities needing fixtures.']);
add('Micro-pave metal surface and gem-radius interpolation','CSMicroPave requires gems, rail curve, base profile and ring radius. It maps gem centers to closest curve parameters and sizes, recalculates curves on dependency changes, creates a micro-pave surface and start/end profiles. CalculateCurves maps arc lengths to a straight line and interpolates local gem radii.',[E('CSBlocks.Surfaces/CSMicroPave.cs','public override bool Update()','CSMicroPave.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Surfaces/CSMicroPave.cs','private bool CalculateCurves','CSMicroPave.CalculateCurves')],K.concat(['MicroPaveProng helpers','dependency change markers']),'local-kernel-required',['Build a micro-pave row with varying gem sizes on a curved shank; compare metal surface and endpoint profiles.','Modify gem size and curve independently and verify interpolated envelope refresh, including missing-radius/profile failure.']);
add('Milgrain point spacing','CSMilgrainPoints computes point count as curve length/(2*size+spacing), samples normalized arc length and nests outputs only for multiple input curves. Invalid curve or pitch below .001 is skipped.',[E('CSBlocks.Transforms/CSMilgrainPoints.cs','private static Point3dList GeneratePointsFromCurve','CSMilgrainPoints.GeneratePointsFromCurve')],K,'local-kernel-required',['Sample a 10mm line with size .1 and spacing .05; compare count and exact point positions including end behavior.','Supply two curves and verify nested array shape, then pitch .0009 and verify skipped output.']);
add('Profile placement on one/two ring rails','CSProfilePlacer2RailXform rejects more than one inner/outside rail, adjusts relative curve direction and length position, wraps closed-rail normalized values once and clamps open rails. It uses normalized arc-length parameters and outputs transform/profile metadata consumed by sweeps.',[E('CSBlocks.Profiles/CSProfilePlacer2RailXform.cs','public override bool Update()','CSProfilePlacer2RailXform.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Profiles/CSProfilePlacer2RailXform.cs','CSUtilGeometry.AdjustRailFromCurve','CSProfilePlacer2RailXform.Update')],K.concat(['profile dictionaries','rail direction/seam conventions']),'local-kernel-required',['Place asymmetric profile at positions -.1, 0, .5, 1 and 1.1 on open/closed two-rail inputs; compare transforms and parameter outputs.','Reverse either rail or supply reference curve and verify frame orientation and side selection.'],['All 13 current/7 old profile node identities remain separate test entries.']);
add('Dome end caps and collar trimming','CSProfileCapRing derives an average profile plane, transforms and centers the profile, picks dome sign from location/orientation, rail-revolves a dome and transforms it back. CSSweepCollarRail locally unscales a rail, intersects a horizontal line at height, trims between extreme hits and extends tangents toward ZX plane.',[E('CSBlocks.Caps/CSProfileCapRing.cs','CSUtilRailRevolve.RailRevolve','CSProfileCapRing.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Collars/CSSweepCollarRail.cs','Intersection.CurveCurve','CSSweepCollarRail.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Collars/CSSweepCollarRail.cs','value2 = value2.Trim','CSSweepCollarRail.Update')],K,'local-kernel-required',['Cap an asymmetric ring profile on opposite ring sides and compare dome direction and thickness.','Trim collar with 2 and >2 intersections, tangent side extensions and height outside bounds; compare rail output and failure modes.']);
add('Bail rails and opening measurement','CSBailRail reads length/opening/pinch/angle/closed and three blend values, removes short segments at .2, repairs bad knots and calls RhinoRepairCurve before building its modified rail. Dedicated outputs provide three parameters and inside height/depth.',[E('CSBlocks.Bails/CSBailRail.cs','public override bool Update()','CSBailRail.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Bails/CSBailRail.cs','RhUtil.RhinoRepairCurve','CSBailRail.Update')],K.concat(['Bail morph/profile helpers']),'local-kernel-required',['Build open/closed bail with pinch and three blend controls; compare opening inside height/depth and sweep placement parameters.','Use an input rail with sub-.2 segments/bad knots; compare repaired rail topology to PC.'],['Bail placer, two-rail side profile, half profile and obsolete variants are in inventory but not individually body-audited.']);
add('Curve offsets with local plane conventions','CSCurveOffset obtains plane/bounds for planar curves, reverses the requested offset sign for that branch, uses OffsetOld closed=true and optionally applies a Z translation carrying transform metadata. This legacy kernel path and sign convention must be retained.',[E('CSBlocks.Curves/CSCurveOffset.cs','value = 0.0 - value','CSCurveOffset.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Curves/CSCurveOffset.cs','CSUtilGeometry.OffsetOld','CSCurveOffset.Update')],K.concat(['CSUtilGeometry.OffsetOld']),'local-kernel-required',['Offset clockwise/counterclockwise planar loops in XY and tilted planes by +/- .2; compare side, curve count and closure.','Offset a curve array with optional Z shift and confirm transform metadata and failure behavior for bad curve.']);
add('Planar curve boolean with first-result selection','CSCurveBoolean repeatedly subtracts each negative curve through RhinoCurveBooleanDifference. When multiple loops are returned it uses array[0], converts back to NURBS and preserves input transform metadata. Empty/failed difference leaves the previous curve.',[E('CSBlocks.Curves/CSCurveBoolean.cs','RhUtil.RhinoCurveBooleanDifference','CSCurveBoolean.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Curves/CSCurveBoolean.cs','array[0].GetNurbForm','CSCurveBoolean.Update')],K,'retain-kernel-result-selection',['Subtract a stripe splitting a positive loop into two islands and compare which first island remains with PC.','Run a nonintersecting and invalid subtraction and verify unchanged input behavior and transform metadata.']);
add('One-, two- and four-rail sweeps with parameters and seam handling','CSSimpleSweep2 gathers rails/profile arrays and optional parameter arrays; with no parameters it calls Sweep2NoParam with seam/maintain-height/closed options, otherwise Sweep2. It rebuilds dynamic output channels for every returned BRep. CSUtilSweepRC Sweep4Profile stores four curve parameters, rematches direction and seam and splits profile into rail-matched pieces.',[E('CSBlocks.Sweeps/CSSimpleSweep2.cs','if (list2.Count == 0 && list3.Count == 0)','CSSimpleSweep2.Update'),E('CSBlocks.Sweeps/CSSimpleSweep2.cs','base.OutputChannels.Clear()','CSSimpleSweep2.Update'),E('CSBlockUtil/CSUtilSweepRC.cs','public bool SetupFromRails','CSUtilSweepRC.Sweep4Profile.SetupFromRails'),E('CSBlockUtil/CSUtilSweepRC.cs','public bool Split(out Curve','CSUtilSweepRC.Sweep4Profile.Split')],K.concat(['CSUtilSweep/CSUtilSweepRC','dynamic output channel identities']),'local-kernel-required',['Sweep asymmetric profiles on open/closed rails with/without explicit parameters and reversed seam; compare surface count, order, normals and channel IDs.','Build four-rail sweep with all four contact points, reverse a section and verify continuity and seam consistency.'],['All 12 current and 2 obsolete sweep registrations require separate fixtures including pipe/revolve and no-profile branches.']);
